# This repo is public. Every rule below is either "this is a secret", "this is
# biometric", or "this is a build artifact nobody should diff". The first two
# categories are the reason the third is written so carefully: a broad rule
# added to keep the diff clean is how the narrow rule protecting a token gets
# quietly widened into uselessness.
#
# `.gitignore` only protects what has not been committed yet. Before flipping a
# repo public, audit the history as well:
#   git log --all --pretty=format: --name-only --diff-filter=A | sort -u

# --- The private half ------------------------------------------------------
# Everything between the markers is BOTH git-ignored and backed up by
# scripts/backup-secrets.sh, which reads this block. That is the point of the
# pairing: a file listed here can never be published by accident, and can never
# be lost by only living on this laptop.
#
# Only the paths are in git, never the contents. Run `scripts/backup-secrets.sh
# --list` to see what a backup would take.
#
# The voice recording is the one irreplaceable entry. Losing it means
# re-recording, and every video after that is in a subtly different voice.
# backup:start
PROFILE.md
PLAN.md
notes/*.md
# Session state: what is live, what is queued, what to check next. Private
# because it carries account performance numbers, and backed up because losing
# it loses the thread.
HANDOVER.md
# Ranked ideas for the Reels and the reasons old ones died. Private for the same
# reason as HANDOVER.md, since every idea is argued from view counts, skip rates
# and follower numbers. The method that produces it is public in
# .claude/skills/reel-council; only the evidence and the decisions are not.
IDEAS.md
.env
data/star_history.json
data/used_repos.json
data/ig_token.json
tools/chatterbox/ref/morten.wav
tools/chatterbox/ref/morten.m4a
# Six candidate spinoff accounts with frame mockups, drawn up 2026-08-25.
# Private for the same reason as IDEAS.md: every score in it is argued from this
# account's own numbers. The directory entry is what keeps git out, including the
# throwaway generator under tools/; the two globs below it are what the backup
# script can actually take, since it only archives files a glob matches.
SPINOFFS.md
notes/spinoffs/
video/src/spinoff/
tools/spinoff/
notes/spinoffs/*.png
notes/spinoffs/*.html
# The Chapter and Verse episodes, which are the only copy of about a day's work
# and existed nowhere but this laptop's disk until 2026-08-26. The directory
# entries above keep git out; only a glob is actually archived, so the source
# was ignored by both git and the backup at once. That is the failure mode this
# whole block exists to prevent, so the globs are listed by extension rather
# than by directory.
video/src/spinoff/*.tsx
tools/spinoff/*.py
notes/spinoffs/*.mp4
notes/spinoffs/tools/*.py
notes/spinoffs/tools/*.html
# The artefacts and voice tracks the episodes render from. Scans and public
# domain images, fetched once and not trivially re-fetchable now that Darwin
# Online sits behind a frameset and gutendex has started answering 503.
video/public/cv-*.jpg
video/public/cv-*.png
video/public/cv-*.wav
# backup:end

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Every variant, because `.env.local` and `.env.backup` are exactly the files
# that get created in a hurry and never thought about again. `.env.example`
# is re-included and is the only one that may ever be tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Keys and certificates. Nothing here should ever produce one, which is the
# point: if a file matches this, something has gone wrong and git staying quiet
# about it is the failure mode to avoid.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Claude Code writes machine-local permissions and paths here. The shared
# settings.json and any project skills are tracked; the .local. ones are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
# Not the dependency source of truth here: requirements.txt is, compiled from
# pyproject.toml. A stray uv.lock left behind by `uv run` puts uv into project
# mode and it re-syncs the venv to the default group, which silently uninstalls
# the dev extras that ruff and pytest live in.
uv.lock
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Pipeline output and persistent state ----------------------------------
# NOTE: `data/*` not `data/` -- git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored
# directory, so the negation below only works if the directory itself is not
# ignored.
#
# data/ is not just noise. It holds ig_token.json, which is a live Instagram
# credential with publishing and messaging rights.
build/
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# TTS + Whisper model weights (~350 MB)
models/

# --- Gateway state ---------------------------------------------------------
# The SQLite file holds conversations with real people, including their
# Instagram-scoped ids. The covers directory is a cache of images already
# uploaded to Instagram. Neither belongs in a public repo, and the database is
# the one that would be a privacy incident rather than an embarrassment.
gateway/dev.sqlite3
gateway/dev.sqlite3-*
gateway/covers/
gateway/state/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal

# --- Node / Remotion -------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
video/out/
video/.remotion/

# Assets the renderer stages for Remotion. Regenerated from build/ on every
# run, so tracking them means a churning binary diff per render.
video/public/*
!video/public/.gitkeep

# --- Voice -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The venv carries torch and is ~3 GB. `ref/` holds recordings of my own voice,
# which are biometric and the one input that makes the clone possible, so they
# stay out of git deliberately rather than by oversight. Losing them means
# re-recording, not a leak. RECORD-THIS.txt is only the passage to read aloud,
# so it is re-included and is safe in public.
tools/chatterbox/.venv/
tools/chatterbox/ref/*
!tools/chatterbox/ref/RECORD-THIS.txt
tools/chatterbox/out/

# Loose audio and video anywhere in the tree. The pipeline writes these under
# build/ and the voice under tools/chatterbox/ref/, both already covered; this
# catches the copy someone drops in the root to listen to it.
*.wav
*.m4a
*.mp3
*.mp4

# --- Editors and OS --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.idea/
*.swp
